# VS Code REST Client — install the 'REST Client' extension, then click 'Send Request'

### Get all parts
GET http://localhost:8080/api/parts

###

### Get low stock parts (at or below per-part reorder threshold)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/parts/low-stock

###

### Get stage summary
GET http://localhost:8080/api/parts/summary

###

### Add a part
POST http://localhost:8080/api/parts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "partName": "Test Filter",
  "supplierName": "Bosch",
  "machineModel": "Excavator X200",
  "stage": "SUPPLIER",
  "stockQuantity": 20,
  "unitCost": 45.00,
  "reorderThreshold": 10,
  "notes": ""
}

###

### Advance part to next stage (replace 1 with real id)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/parts/1/advance

###

### Update a part
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/parts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "partName": "Test Filter",
  "supplierName": "Bosch",
  "machineModel": "Excavator X200",
  "stage": "SUPPLIER",
  "stockQuantity": 50,
  "unitCost": 45.00,
  "reorderThreshold": 10,
  "notes": ""
}

###

### Get part history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/parts/1/history

###

### Delete a part
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/parts/1

###

### Swagger UI (open in browser)
# http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html

### H2 database console (open in browser)
# http://localhost:8080/h2-console
